Craig,


&nbsp;


I have been forwarded this exchange and am troubled that the fees allocated to me are wrong (as they are with some of the other CT members).&nbsp; I imagine that this may be a concern for you also if you are going to
 be the one asked to sign the statement of truth on the costs schedule!&nbsp;


&nbsp;


I understand that I have been paid £1,745,195.60 (at the discounted CFA rate).&nbsp; At a notional non-discounted rate, but without any of the success fee uplift (which can't be passed on), the amount would be £2,181.494.50.&nbsp;
 &nbsp;I don't therefore at the moment u/stand where the figure in the spreadsheet of £2,298,065.60 comes from.


&nbsp;


Andrew

