The other thing that is not entirely clear to me is whether the spreadsheet contains the costs relating to the jurisdiction/strike-out stage (including the appeal to the CA) or whether it excludes those costs (which I think
 were claimed to be in the 20m region, with the CA ordering a payment on account of 10m).
If they have been excluded, then no credit is to be given to BHP for the 10m interim payment that they have already made.
But if they have been included in the spreadsheet, then we’ll have to give credit/take account of the 10m already paid by BHP when we apply for the interim payment at the December hearing.
&nbsp;

