rised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;30 October 2025 16:03To:&nbsp;Craig Shuttleworth &lt;craig@kastlesolicitors.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;; Holly Hampton &lt;hhampton@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Federica Lombardi &lt;flombardi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Report&nbsp;Hi all&nbsp;Just catching up - was in court again today. Helena will shortly share the letter with some edits proposed by Fergal from Clydes. It will also address the position on Tom. Let's consider once that lands.&nbsp;Matt - thanks for your email separately. I'm taking the liberty to relay Giles W KC advice re consultant point:&nbsp;There is no inherent regulatory bar on a solicitor at another firm being engaged to work as a consultant on a particular matter.&nbsp; From a conduct of litigation perspective, I don’t see any problem with this.&nbsp;There are of course a raft of issues that any such consultancy arrangement would need to address, e.g. how to deal with conflicts of interest, lines of supervision/responsibility, client consent, the terms of the consultancy engagement, and no doubt various other issues.&nbs