ult of this ruling, he revised the timetable for the defendants to issue any applications for security for costs and ordered that the claimants have until 12th December to confirm to the defendants their level of coverage. If 64% is not achieved at such time, the defendants will issue a security for costs application by 19th December. If such applications are made for the sole reason that PG has not obtained 64%, PG will lose those applications, and the cost of that will far outweigh the cost of the expected premiums (not to mention wasting valuable human resources required for the running of the case). By way of comparison, 13 applications were made against PG to disclose the funding documents. The defendants' aggregate statement of costs comes to over £500k. The cost of any security for costs application will be substantially higher if done on a similar scale.&nbsp;We attach hereto the following documents for Gramercy’s review and approval:&nbsp;(i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; NBI from Toremis(ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Overarching priority deed regulating the cross-collateralisation. Please note that this draft is based on the existing wrapper deed (subject to the specific terms agreed with Toremis).(iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Insurance policy terms(iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amendments and Restatement to the Individual Priorities Deeds. The ones for the remaining cases will follow.&nbsp;Please let us know if you have any questions. We appreciate it if you could prioritise this, given the court deadlines mentioned above.&nbsp;Thank you.&nbsp;Kind regards&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom:&nbsp;Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&