 term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 10 October 2025 09:53To: Neil Pigott &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Hi Neil,&nbsp;I am incorporating some of your suggested edits and will send over shortly.&nbsp;Many thanks Helena &nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Neil Pigott &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 10 October 2025 09:14To: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Tom,&nbsp;Have you included our suggested edits sent yesterday or are those going to be added please?&nbsp;I will review in the meantime but please let me know on the above.&nbsp;Many thanks,&nbsp;Neil&nbsp;Neil&nbsp;PigottPartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1005|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;75&nbsp;5741&nbsp;2828E:&nbsp;&nbsp;neil.pigott@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInPallas Partners LLP is a limited liability partnership registered in England with registered number OC437491, and is authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority of England and Wales (“SRA”) with SRA number 826251. A list of names of the members is available for inspection at our registered address at&nbsp;110 Bishopsgate, London, EC2N 4AY.&nbsp;The word “partner” denotes a member of&nbsp;Pallas Partners LLP&nbsp;or an employee or consultant with equivalent standing and qualifications.&nbsp;Pallas Partners (US) LLP is a limited liability partnership established in Delaware and registered in New York, located at 75 Rockefeller Plaza, New York, NY, 10019.&nbsp;Attorneys practicing law with Pallas Partners (US) LLP are admitted to practice in New York and their professional conduct is regulated by the New York Rules of Professional Conduct.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;This email (and any attachments) is confidential and may also be legally privileged and is intended solely for the use of the individual or entity addressed above. If you are not the intended recipient, please immediately notify the sender, then delete it from your system. You should not copy it or use it for any purpose, nor disclose its contents to any other person. Please also note that emails sent or received may be monitored to ensure compliance with the law and with our policies.&nbsp;Further regulatory information can be found in the Legal Notices which appear on our website at&nbsp;https://www.pallasllp.com/legal.​​​​From: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 10 October 2025 08:14To: Neil Pigott &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Morning All &nbsp;I have slightly tweaked the letter as attached (amend for repetition and raise one comment). On Theo’s comments (focussing on those that require further thought and comment our side)&nbsp;I haven't been party to the detail of Gramercy's arrangements with PG save that I have seen what is in Alinia 1, so can't help on whether this detail is correct/comprehensive. What is important to say is that given the ATE shortfall there is a real risk that the funding agreements between PG and Gramercy will eventually be disclosed to the court. It is critical that this account presents a straightforward and accurate picture of Gramercy's funding.We are checking internally to make sure that we are comfortable with the statement that “the September ($30m) Tranche can contractually be used only for the NOx Group Litigations.” I believe this is correct on the basis that the facility must be spent in line with the funder approved budget and that budget only provides for spend against the Nox litigation and proportionate share of firm operating costs, but I am not sure how clear this will be to demonstrate through the actual contracts.&nbsp;You need to be careful that this is absolutely aligned with what is said about the Gramercy additional funding in Alicia Alinia’s recent First Witness Statement. Particularly she says the 30m additional is reserved to only be spent on these proceedings while the 65m is also for wider overheads. We need to be consistent here.@Neil Pigott ?&nbsp;Are there any other funders of the litigation, including historic, who might be said to contribute to the Claimant’s costs? I distantly recall I have seen mention of another funder - but is that historic?We said the below in Tom’s March witness statement, this would have been in relation to NorthWall. &nbsp;The funds provided by Gramercy were used, in part, to repay previous debt finance provided to Pogust Goodhead, which has been superseded by the funding.&nbsp;We have not disclosed t