Hi All, &nbsp;We’re having some difficulty with the lawyers currently on their notice period who are trying every which way to get out of their notice periods by quoting various sections of the SRA and pointing to misrep. We’ve managed, successfully, to dampen their efforts based on the Gallagher approach of a repudiatory breach based on the G3 deal and now their efforts are focused on demanding that we tell everyone that they’re in their notice period despite us consistently telling them that any communication needs to be well coordinated and in an effort to preserve the firm and the clients interests. &nbsp;I’d be grateful for your help in drafting a suitable response to all of them as they continue to play these games despite having professional obligations. &nbsp;Many thanksA&nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From: Alicia Alinia Sent: 25 September 2025 16:29To: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Signature Application - Action required&nbsp;Hi Mike, &nbsp;Thanks for your email. &nbsp;We’ll consider all the points you’ve raised and revert as soon as possible. Anna will be responding on the specific points as they relate to the correspondence from Renault.&nbsp;ThanksA&nbsp;From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 14:24To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Signature Application - Action requiredImportance: High&nbsp;Dear Board,&nbsp;In follow up to my email at 12.52 today, I am writing to ask for immediate attention to be given to addressing my (and the other case leaves) employment position to the Defendants, Court, clients and any other relevant stake holders.&nbsp;As Signature's draft application points out at 8(b)(iii) - a letter was sent out yesterday, naming me as the PG contact.&nbsp;&nbsp;That I am named as the contact appears to have been an administrative oversight, and I put no blame on the sender of the letter, however this has now lead to a misleading position, or what will be a mislead position if not immediately clarified, underpinning the concerns I had regarding paragraph 27 of the letter sent to the Defendants on Tuesday 23 September (see my email at 12.52 today and my suggestion at 15.59 on 23 September).&nbsp;&nbsp;The SRA Code of Conduct at 1.4 says &quot;You do not mislead or attempt to mislead your clients, the court&nbsp;or others, either by your own acts or omissions or allowing or being complicit in the acts or omissions of others (including your client)&quot;&nbsp;By this letter having gone out, and by repeat correspondence continuing to go out in my name on the Ford and Volvo litigations, and the names of the other case leads, without appropriate context that we are working our notice, I have real concerns that the firm is (and I am) in breach of 1.4 of the code of conduct. This applies not only to correspondence to the Defendant firms, but also to clients and any external parties.&nbsp;This requires immediate attention, especially in respect of my position.&nbsp;&nbsp;SL have asked for a response by 4pm. Without wanting to force the hands of the board, I must be insistent that the below (or clarification of that nature) is sent before that deadline to clarify the position:&nbsp;&quot;Pogust Goodhead are considering your application and will respond in due course.&nbsp;&nbsp;As an immediate step, and to address 8(b)(iii) in your application, we confirm categorically that MR Burke does not have conduct of these Pan NOx Litigations. The inclusion of Mr Burke's details in the letter sent to the Defendants on 24 September which named Michael Burke as a &quot;contact&quot;, this was an oversight, and this does not indicate that Mr Burke has conduct of these Pan NOx Litigations on behalf of Pogust Goodhead and Pogust Goodhead's clients. For absolute clarity, Mr Burke does not have conduct of the Pan-NOx Litigations on behalf of Pogust Goodhead.&nbsp;&nbsp;Mr Burke currently has conduct of the Ford NOx Litigation, and the Volvo NOx Litigation, as part of the Pan NOx Litigations. The overall supervision of the Pan-NOx Litigations for Pogust Goodhead will be confirmed in due course as requested in your application.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We also take this opportunity to advise the Defendants, that Mr Burke has formally tendered his resignation with Pogust Goodhead, as of 15 September 2025, and he is currently working his notice period, the end date which is to be confirmed. Correspondence will be sent directly to the Defendants in those Litigations as soon as possible.&quot;&nbsp;This needs to be sent as soon as possible. I imagine this may be an opportune moment to advise on the other Case Leads and I am happy for this to be incorporated, but the clarity on my position needs to be dealt with immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344&nbsp;"}

