Dear all,


Thank you for your kind responses to my email last week. I write with a further update to the Ford NOx Emissions
 Litigation (the “Ford Litigation”), and the Pan-NOx Litigation generally (the “Litigation”):

Role as Lead Solicitors&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Pogust Goodhead, the firm, has applied to step away from its role as &quot;Lead Solicitor&quot; in the Lead Case and Additional Lead
 Cases which are proceeding to the PDD Trial, on a temporary basis only. This application was partly heard at the PTR yesterday but the Court has not yet confirmed in it in an Order. Set out below is information on: i) what the role of Lead Solicitor is; ii)
 the reasons why the firm believes this step is necessary, including the advice of counsel; and iii) what this will mean for the firm, and the Ford Litigation as well as the PDD Trial.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
The firm must advise you that this step has not been taken due to the merits of the Litigation changing. We remain confident
 in the strength of the case and are confident in a successful conclusion.&nbsp; The firm stepping down does not affect the substantive work it is doing for the Ford Litigation and PDD Trial.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
The intention to step down temporarily as Lead Solicitors is in the Lead Cases only, in fact, to ensure the cases are protected
 and the PDD Trial proceeds without disruption.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;

·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
What is the role of Lead Solicitor?&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;
The role of Lead Solicitor is a Court-appointed role. Currently, Pogust Goodhead and Leigh Day are appointed as joint Lead
 Solicitors for this Litigation. The role of Lead Solicitors formally entitles the firm, jointly with Leigh Day, to manage the Litigation on behalf of all Claimants, not just those who formally instruct this firm.&nbsp; The role of Lead Solicitor is set out in paragraph
 10 of the Ford Group Litigation Order.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Pogust Goodhead are intending to step down temporarily as Lead Solicitor in the Lead Cases only, and Leigh Day will remain
 the sole Lead Solicitor for the Litigation during the course of the PDD Trial. Pogust Goodhead will remain Lead Solicitors in respect of the remaining Non-Lead Cases. Pogust Goodhead regaining their position as Lead Solicitors will be subject to Court approval.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;

·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
Why does the firm believe it needs to step down as Lead Solicitor for the purposes of the PDD Trial?&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The firm's decision arises following recent reports in the press regarding the firm, including internal management changes
 (including my resignation). While Pogust Goodhead is confident that recent changes will strengthen the firm and its governance structures, and that questions regarding ancillary matters do not raise any concerns as to the firm’s ability to conduct the litigation,
 the firm intends to step down temporarily in order to ensure that those reports, and the resulting attempts by the Defendants to exploit them, do not distract from the upcoming PDD Trial and derail the procedural timetable in any way, and ensure that we stay
