If the Defendants' objection is upheld, then the collateral use restrictions on the Claimants remain; but they were never in place for any other parties.&nbsp; For example, if an amber document appears on the EPE, a third party or journalist is immediately allowed
 to quote it.&nbsp; If an application is made seven days later to restrict collateral use, that only affects the Claimants.




I take the point that us handing documents to third parties is collateral use, but that is the only way that they can get hold of them, i.e. in practice the Claimants' collateral use restrictions are in fact placed upon third parties, even though para 12(b)(ii)
 specifically only applies to the Claimants (as argued at length at the DDH).




