Subject:&nbsp;Counsel CFAs

&nbsp;
Hi Anna, Michael
&nbsp;
Please see attached an example GLO specific counsel CFA as drafted by George McDonald.
&nbsp;
We have had a few rumblings from counsel that they want these all signed this week ahead of the PDD trial.
&nbsp;
There were a few outstanding points, so I had a brief conversation with George just now to resolve these.
&nbsp;
In summary:
&nbsp;


Paragraph 10: George noted the potential for disparity between this and how clients are defined in the GLOs. He noted that, as long as all clients on the Group Register are represented by firms who have, or will
 shortly have, entered into a corresponding Agency Agreement, this should be fine. His concern was if there are clients represented by firms who will not be entering into the AA. I told him that not all firms have signed but that they will eventually be party
 to the AAs.
Paragraph 15: This needs to reflect to cost sharing provisions in each GLO and will therefore need to be amended on the basis of each.
&nbsp;
George suggested that, to appease counsel and to allow him to finalise the remaining CFAs due to the nuance of paragraph 15, we should circulate the attached draft version
 with the clerks this week (i.e., tomorrow). He said we should state that the only change will be paragraph 15, and it will be similar, if not the same, terms, but that we still need to check and redraft where necessary. The redrafting will be done by George
 over the weekend so we should be able to tell them we will have final versions for all GLOs early next week.
&nbsp;
Circulating this draft will be done in the hopes that getting something out – and also allowing for an opportunity to provide comments – will give us the breathing room
 needed to this final point checked over the weekend.
&nbsp;
It is our intention to circulate this draft
tomorrow morning.&nbsp;Please could you let us know if you are happy with this so that we can do so?
&nbsp;
Separately, Zoe O’Sullivan KC and Jennifer Meech at Serle Court have not yet been sent the Pan NOx CFA and we will circulate that to them tomorrow morning too, however
 we are just noting for completeness that LD will be the only signatory to this.
&nbsp;
We look forward to hearing from you.
