Hi Carolina &nbsp;Please see the statement attached. &nbsp;In case helpful you can find all the funding disclosure applications and accompanying docs in this folder:  [For Counsel] Funding Disclosure Applications&nbsp;Let me know if there’s anything else I can do to help. &nbsp;Best Jess &nbsp;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 06 November 2025 12:44To: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Disclosure application - AA2 WS&nbsp;@Jessica Fechner Could you let me know where I can find the witness statement that is defined as Boddy 11, pls? The questions addressed to me refer to that document. &nbsp;Regarding tax, I believe the implications can be materially significant, as the basic premise of our financial model and our financial statements is that the facilities are true loans. &nbsp;I am not an accountant or tax lawyer, but claiming that the funding is a fee-sharing arrangement would automatically exclude it from being a loan as a business-to-business structure. We should speak to David Kan and Donatas. I think they’ve discussed this with auditors and big 4 firms, so I would not take the risk without further investigation. &nbsp;We should consider whether characterizing this as a fee-sharing arrangement would automatically exclude it from being treated as a loan under a business-to-business structure. My concern is that this might create room for potential inconsistencies with our previous statements. &nbsp;I will call Matt and try to bring DK in as we spoke on Teams.&nbsp;Kind regards &nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 06 November 2025 04:17To: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Disclosure application - AA2 WS&nbsp;Carolina&nbsp;I've raised the two points with Pallas - I dont think PACCAR is an issue and Gramercy have confirmed they are fine to concede the point.&nbsp;&nbsp;Im not sure on what basis being a funder re-classifies the credit agreement as anything other than a loan but I am not a tax specialist so defo could be wrong - this is not something Pallas can speak to either I suspect and we may need to take the risk.&nbsp;Please can I have the information I requested about Fulcrum/Locke asap this morning so that we can start to finalise - please can this be prioritised.&nbsp;Thanks​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Wednesday, November 5, 2025 10:50 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Disclosure application - AA2 WS &nbsp;Thanks, Anna. I will review the doc in more detail, but the main question that Pallas can help with, if they haven’t considered this yet, is whether taking the position of a “funder” under CPR 25.28(b) could impact the treatment of the credit agreement and its characterisation as a fee-sharing arrangement, as considered in PACCAR. If there is an overlap between these concepts, it may be difficult for Gramercy to accept CPR 25.28(b), depending on the risk that the credit agreement could be deemed unenforceable. I am not familiar with the details of the case law, but it may be worth looking/discussing it with Boies if Pallas hasn’t done so yet. There are a few clauses in the credit agreement pasted below where PG represented that the Credit Agreement is not a fee sharing agreement for the PACCAR purpose.&nbsp;Another important aspect of this is tax consequences. If assuming the position of a “funder” under CPR 25.28(b) would result in the credit agreement being reclassified as something other than a loan or debt, this could adversely affect the deductibility of interest for corporation tax purposes. &nbsp;&nbsp;6.30. 58AA Courts and Legal Services Act 1990. Each Borrower shall not, andshall cause each of the Credit Parties and their respective Affiliates not to, directly or indirectly, (a)challenge the enforceability of this Agreement, any Credit Document, the G1 Facility CreditAgreement, any other G1 Facility Funding Documentation, the G2 Facility Credit Agreement or anyother G2 Facility Funding Documentation for any reason whatsoever, including by reference tos.58AA Courts and Legal Services Act or any analogous law, regulation or theory, including but notlimited to by reference to R (PACCAR) v Competition Appeal Tribunal [2023] UKSC 28 or (b) takethe position that this Agreement (or any portion hereof) is not governed exclusively by, or notconstrued, determined and enforced exclusively in accordance with, the laws of the State of NewYork (without regard to conflict of laws principles thereof exclusively by New York).&nbsp;8.24. Relationship Between Secured Parties and Borrowers. Each Credit Partywaives any right to bring any private cause of action or any suit of any nature against any Lender or the Lender Representative (or any of their respective officers, directors, employees, agents orrepresentatives) in connection with any alleged violation of any applicable Disciplinary Rules. EachCredit Party waives any right to assert any defense to the payment of the Obligations based on aviolation of any applicable Disciplinary Rules. Each Credit Party acknowledges that it has enteredinto this Agreement and all Credit Documents with the Secured Parties, each of which is a nonlawyer.The Borrowers and the Secured Parties hereby agree that this Agreement and the otherCredit Documents evidence a loan and financing agreement wherein the Lenders are providingfinancing to the Borrowers, and the Borrowers represent to the Secured Parties that the contemplatedtransactions do not constitute in any manner a fee sharing agreement between any of the SecuredParties and the Borrowers, and it is the intent of the Borrowers to strictly comply with the applicableDisciplinary Rules. The Borrowers and the Secured Parties acknowledge and agree that no SecuredParty has a contingent or other interest in the outcome of any Case. The Secured Parties shall haveno direct contact with the Clients, and the Secured Parties shall have no influence or control overthe litigation strategy with respect to any Case. The Secured Parties shall not interfere, and theBorrowers shall not allow any interference by any Secured Party, with the attorney-clientrelationship in connection with any Client, Case, or otherwise. (…)”&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 05 November 2025 16:49To: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Disclosure application - AA2 WS&nbsp;Hi all&nbsp;I've just been speaking to Helena about the below. She suggested that @Carolina Koschdoski de Souza&nbsp;might be able to assist quicker with the information required for this witness statement. This witness statement must be served by 4pm Friday 7th&nbsp;(this week) so we really need this info tonight/tomorrow. See the yellow highlights specifically. Also (appreciating you are juggling an enormous workload) if the A&amp;R execution has to slip so we can finalise this statement I would much rather that as this is court ordered and we can explain the timing.&nbsp;@Carolina Koschdoski de Souza&nbsp;give me a call if you want to discuss.&nbsp;ThanksAnna&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, November 5, 2025 3:04 PMTo:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;FW: Disclosure application - AA2 WS &nbsp;Hi all&nbsp;Following up on the email from Pallas yesterday asking for input on the funding disclosure statement, would it be possible to get your input on these points this afternoon? &nbsp;I attach the latest draft of the statement for reference.&nbsp;In case helpful to get the ball rolling I have tried to allocate the relevant points below but please do let me know if there is someone else better placed to answer.&nbsp;Also just a minor formatting point, but just to note that the paragraph numbering seems to have gone awry in that it restarts from 23 in Section IV so some of the paragraph references are confusing. I will flag this to Pallas on response.&nbsp;ThanksJess&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom:&nbsp;Amy Hobbs &lt;Amy.Hobbs@pallasllp.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;04 November 2025 13:43To:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Erika Saluzzo &lt;esaluzzo@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Disclosure application - AA2 WS&nbsp;CAUTION: This ema