nd 21 October 2025 (see para 27) – I am looking into thisd)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; whether PG has disclosed financial statements/ Fulcrum and Locke funding documents (see para 28) @Helena Yearwood, @Alicia Aliniae)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;status of the funding with Fulcrum and Locke (see para 28) @Helena Yearwoodf)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; what the loans in WJB/538-540 are and whether any of them are prior Gramercy funding (see para 31) – See extract of relevant pages attached. @Tom Crow are you able to confirm?g)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; whether we ever informed the Defendants of when the Gramercy funding started in correspondence (see para 31) @Helena Yearwood are you aware of this? I can also have a look through previous correspondence.2)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Populate Opus references as required throughout / let Pallas know which documents are not on Opus for Pallas to exhibit – I will deal with this.3)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Provide Pallas with the following documents:a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; a copy of NOX1D12/5 I’ll share thisb)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; a copy of the letter Anna mentioned following her review of the statement (see para 26) regarding the allegation that PG have set unreasonably tight deadlines in correspondence throughout the trial phase. I will find thisc)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;timestamp of the emails attaching (i) McGuire Woods letter dated 1 October 2025 (see para 26.2) Timestamp 20:05 ; and (ii) Quinn letter dated 22 October 2023 (see para 26.4) I’m looking into this4)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Keep Pallas updated with progress of discussions to secure further ATE cover @Helena Yearwood&nbsp;– maybe we could provide Pallas with a status update at the end of the day today?&nbsp;Many thanks,Amy&nbsp;Amy&nbsp;Hobbs​​​​AssociateT: +44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1056|M: +44&nbsp;7751&nbsp;928&nbsp;570E:&nbsp; amy.hobbs@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;Londo