 that is being sought - this aligns with the approach Leigh Day is taking. I don't yet have pro rated cover per defendant: @Tom Crow&nbsp;is that something you could assist with please?&nbsp;60% of the Defendants incurred costs (including those from CMH1 and CMH2, the costs of cost budgeting from both CMH1 and CMH2, and the Non-Tranche 3 Quantum costs).100% of the Defendants Tranche 2 (£90.5 million) and First General approved future costs (£19.25 million)Defendants Tranche 3 approved future costs up to 31 July 2026, broken down as follows:100% of CMC, Selection of Sample Claimants, Individual Statements of Case, Disclosure, Witness Statements, and PTR71% of the Tranche 3 Co-Ordination Costs (12.5 out of 17.5 months)Trial Preparation: We had been considering seeking between 33% and 50%. However, Leigh Day is seeking 50%, and we consider a more conservative approach is appropriate in light of the scrutiny. If we go with 50% this would add c. £1.5 million LOI which we can accommodate in the budget. &nbsp;Defendants Second General approved future costs up to 31 July 2026, broken down as follows:44% of GLO Management CostsFortnightly Meetings to September 2026 at 67%T3 Expert Reports/2G ADR: Figures based on Claimant offers. 100% of £10.2m for expert reports, and 44% of £1.8m for ADR. Leigh Day have based their approach on agreed figures, with the following exceptions: &nbsp;where not agreed, Defendants counteroffer, and where no counteroffer, Claimants offer).&nbsp;BestAnna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent: Wednesday, October 22, 2025 8:08 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ 