Theo, Simon&nbsp;Further to Anna’s email please see attached: PG letter dated 10 October re ATE &amp; funding as sent (with appendices)PG’s holding response dated 20 October to the Defendants in response to their letters of 17 OctoberLetter from Gramercy (BSF) dated 20 October in response to the Defendants letters of 17 OctoberLetter from Hogan Lovells dated 20 October in response to PG’s letter of 10 October &nbsp;Kind RegardsJess &nbsp;Jessica Fechner (she/her)Associate (England &amp; Wales qualified) Amsterdam &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 21 October 2025 13:57To: T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Theo, Simon&nbsp;Thank you both for your input in relation to 10 October letter. Simon - I understand you are in a heavy hearing at the moment - best of luck.&nbsp;&nbsp;Theo - we received several letters from Ds about the ATE and funding info disclosure (all within 1.5hrs on Friday evening). Besides a holding response, we are yet to respond substantively. There is a draft response in the works, which we will share today/tomorrow. In the meantime, I wanted to bring this to your attention - not least because any application for disclosure etc will be made 24th&nbsp;October. I've attached the relevant letters and the team will share the draft response once ready. Grateful for you input at such time. In addition, as will have been obvious to you both, we are in the process of sorting additional ATE and the team can update with details/timings.&nbsp;@Jessica Fechner&nbsp;please could you share (as sent) 10 October letter, holding response and check I have not omitted any correspondence on this topic.&nbsp;BestAnna&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Thursday, October 9, 2025 10:09 PMTo:&nbsp;Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;B.Williams@4newsquare.com &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Dear Tom,&nbsp;Please see attached a draft of the letter with my suggested amendments and comments.&nbsp;The most important point here is to make sure that what is said about PG’s funding agreements is accurate and not misleading by omission, because anything that isn’t quite right (or a relevant funding arrangement not included) will doubtless be seized on down the line.&nbsp;On the ATE assumptions, my views are as follows (and I know these are shared by Simon):&nbsp;We think that future costs for ADR and Experts should be included in the relevant expenditure calculations. Despite not having been assessed by the court yet, those costs would be incurred within the relevant period and therefore will be taken into account when assessing of sufficiency of cover. It would be reasonable at this stage to take the Claimants’ offers against those phases as the starting point for what we say is required, but we must recognise that leaving those phases out altogether isn’t going to be defensible before the court. So if para 9a and 9b are to go into the letter (and I can see they may be needed for now if the position on sufficiency of cover is to be maintained) we need to accept internally that there will need to be movement on that point (and additional cover) if the position on ATE sufficiency is to be maintained before the court.&nbsp;Similarly, we don’t think there is a strong case for downgrading the % of incurred costs by 10%. Again, if this is to go into the letter we ought to treat it internally as a holding position while you look to increase cover.&nbsp;We agree that it is not sensible to disclose in the letter that you are looking to increase cover. Most importantly, that essentially amounts to a concession that what you have is insufficient - and additionally, as you point out, you may not be able to secure further cover and we don’t want to box ourselves in.&nbsp;I hope that helps. I am around tomorrow morning if needed until around 1pm.&nbsp;Many thanks,&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;Barclay​​​​BarristerDirect&nbsp;+442078222100&nbsp;Mobile&nbsp;+447411&nbsp;731074&nbsp;Chambers&nbsp;+442078222000&nbsp;4&nbsp;New&nbsp;Square&nbsp;Chambers​Lincoln's&nbsp;Inn,&nbsp;London&nbsp;WC2A&nbsp;3RJFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;YouTube | LinkedIn​Discover&nbsp;our Events&nbsp;Privilege and Confidentiality Notice:This email is private as between the sender and the intended recipient. The information contained in this message and any file that may be attached to it are confidential between those parties and may be privileged. Any other party who receives it in error is not permitted to read, use, copy, discuss or pass on the information contained in either the message or its attachments, nor are they entitled to take any action in reliance on the contents. Therefore, if you are not the intended recipient you are kindly requested to contact me immediately by telephone on the numbers given above.Members of 4 New Square Chambers are regulated by the Bar Standards Board.NOTE TO SOLICITORS: ALL PAPERS RECEIVED FOR MEMBERS OF CHAMBERS WILL BE SENT FOR SECURE SHREDDING&nbsp;UPON COMPLETION OF WORK&nbsp;UNLESS YOU SPECIFICALLY REQUEST THEIR RETURN.From: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Thursday, 9 October 2025 at 19:39To: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;, Simon Teasdale &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: Benjamin Williams KC &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;, Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2EXTERNAL EMAIL+Simon Teasdale&nbsp;Hi Theo&nbsp;Thank you for your time earlier and agreeing to provide comment on this letter. If you could please provide your thoughts on the entirety of the letter it would be greatly appreciated.&nbsp;I attach the latest draft of the letter which amends the funding disclosure section to align it more closely with witness statements recently submitted to court.&nbsp;We discussed with Simon yesterday some of the assumptions and caveats we are making in our calculations of projected expenditure to July 2026 (when we expect to receive a decision on PDD). It would be helpful to confirm your /Simon’s views on us making these statements in the letter:&nbsp;Para 9a confirms that costs for the ADR/Settlement phase has not been included in the expenditure calculations as they have not yet been approvedPara 9b confirms that costs for the Expert Reports phase have not been included in the expenditure calculations as they have not yet been approvedPara 13 confirms we are reducing the percentages applied to claimed incurred costs and costs of cost budgeting, the rationale being provided in para 16 (i.e. they are disproportionate and distort the sufficiency analysis)&nbsp;As discussed, these assumptions around calculating expenditure to the decision on PDD, which we believe are reasonable, help to demonstrate that we currently have sufficient cover. Once these points are factored into the calculations it is likely that the shortfall in ATE cover to July 26 will increase.&nbsp;Internally, we are working toward increasing our