e of the trial, is unhelpful and distressing, and significantly adversely impacts our ability to focus on the trial.&nbsp; It also does not make sense to exclude from meetings about trial strategy the PG case leads who have been responsible for trial preparation and strategy for years (and still are responsible).&nbsp; Please include us in all similar meetings.&nbsp;We are concerned that the very nature of the proposed secondment signals to the Court and Defendants that there are in fact legitimate concerns over funder control; it begs the question why would the secondment be necessary if there was nothing to worry about?&nbsp; It therefore risks exacerbating the problem it pretends to solve.&nbsp;It seems to us (including Sarah) that the most sensible solution is to engage in constructive discussions directly with us so as to negate impact on the PDD Trial and quantum work streams as far as possible.&nbsp;Please let us know your availability for a meeting to discuss.&nbsp; That meeting should ideally be today, given that we understand a witness statement explaining the secondment is to be served this evening, taking into account availability.&nbsp;Michael, Priyanka, Sarah, Matt, Georgie​​​​Matt&nbsp;Hunt(He/Him)Legal&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;697&nbsp;"}

