Hi Carol &nbsp;This won’t happen until next year&nbsp;The request to Willis is being made because we know that the Security for costs application is coming (I believe January 2026), and we need to know whether there is any capacity in the market and what the pricing is in case the D’s are successful in their application&nbsp;Our argument is that it is unreasonable to request that the claimants increase their indemnity when we have sufficient cover to last (per current calculations but these will get slightly worse) to at least Jul 26. &nbsp;It is far from certain at the moment whether we will need further cover, if there is further cover available, and what that further cover will cost&nbsp;We will include a placeholder in the budget for the next runthrough with Nick, will flag to him that we need to consider this in the context of 3PF, anything else? (and would you want to be in on that part of the discussion?)&nbsp;Tom&nbsp;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708From: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 14:04To: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;If this is going ahead, we need to start the talks with G asap because of&nbsp;budget and Third Party Fees, unless this is being dealt separately. &nbsp;@Helena Yearwood can you keep us posted of Willis response pls? &nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 07:02To: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: FW: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 10:57To: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: Fw: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;All - see below for visibility.​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Tuesday, September 30, 2025 10:25 AMTo: James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;jonathan.simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jamie Macfarlane &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation &nbsp;Dear James and Jonathan,I hope you're well.I am writing regarding the Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation, specifically regarding the viability of securing additional LOI coverage through further excess layer insurance policies.Following the handing down of the judgment (10th September 2025) after the Second Costs Management Hearing (15-16 July 2025), the Defendants have revisited their position on applications for security for costs. We have therefore undertaken a further review of the potential adverse costs resulting from the Tranche 3 Quantum Trial and the Second General Budget.&nbsp;Previously, our assessment of ATE sufficiency was calculated on the following basis:60% of the Defendants’ claimed incurred costs;60% of the Defendants’ claimed budgeted costs; and100% of approved future costs to Spring 2026.Given the level of incurred costs&nbsp;and the criticisms between Defendants regarding their figures, we consider that the sufficiency calculation can be revised downwards without materially affecting the adequacy of coverage. We propose the following revised basis:50% of the Defendants’ claimed incurred costs;50% of the Defendants’ claimed budgeted costs; and100% of approved future costs to 31 July 2026.On this revised basis, the following GLOs fall below the proposed coverage threshold:&nbsp;Mercedes&nbsp;-£953,580.35Ford-£838,961.27Renault-Nissan-£2,535,219.93PCD-£149,635.79Toyota-£136,927.40&nbsp;We would be grateful for your confirmation on whether additional excess layer coverage can be secured for these cases, specifically for&nbsp;Mercedes, Ford, and Renault-Nissan.We look forward to hearing from you as soon as possible.Kind regards,&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Sarah&nbsp;BinghamLegal&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7484&nbsp;085&nbsp;187&nbsp;"}

