Hi Helena,
&nbsp;
I have spoken to Toremis this morning. In summary:

They are likely to be able to offer terms here, subject to a few points:


Merits – they pass on their thanks to Counsel for the email note.
 They do however require a bit more detail on merits – given Counsel are in trial, they have asked if Anna (or another case lead who is over all the matters) would be able to expand on the merits advice on a call with them?Limit requests – please could Tom also join the call as they have
 some supplemental queries as to how those limit requests have been calculated? Overall they want a deeper dive into the extent there are any headroom in these figures.

Their likely offer:

As Counsel’s note mentions, not all the cases are of uniform risk level. To address this – they have suggested a form of cross-collateralisation
 agreement that would sit over the eight top-up policies. Would this in principle be acceptable to PG? I note there are already the BHP reimbursement deed and the wrapper agreement that relate to the proceeds on these matters, which will need to be taken into
 account here. Having a cross-collateralisation agreement in place would push the pricing offered downwards.Pricing – it is likely to be relatively expensive given they are insuring these matters during a trial and so the upfront premium is likely
 to begin with a “2”. They would be willing to split this into say two payments (the latter of which would be payable in any event) but splitting the payments would increase the overall price e.g. 24% ROL upfront or 2x 14% ROL staggered payments (NB these numbers
 are just illustrative rather than the pricing that Toremis will provide). By way of comparison, where pricing can be offered during trial we have seen it be offered at 30+%.
If point 1 and 2 are acceptable, would we be able to set up the requested call with Toremis this week?
